        "originFactionId": "fac-japan",
        "generationId": "3",
        "classificationId": "heavy_assault",
        "productionStatus": "limited",
        "availability": "restricted",
        "origin": "canon",
        "lore": "Canon prototype heavy battle tank (HT-type14) from Exogularity. The JGSDF began the Yaegaki Plan after the Yakumo Plan's attempt to reproduce the A-10 stalled on advanced materials. It used combat data from the BETA of Megalith. TSF arm manipulators and carbon actuators let it switch between a tank mode for travel and a semi-humanoid mode for fighting. A crew of three runs it through an indirect thought-control system. Its size limits turning and urban use, but it was adopted on the promise of lighter frame materials. Mitsubishi as maker and generation 3 are assumptions; the wiki gives neither.",
        "attribution": "inferred",
        "publishStatus": "published"
      }
